<div class="private-ref">
  <p class="box-label">Private Internal Reference / Not for Circulation</p>
  <p>One quiet pointer for your thinking, held carefully and not for wider circulation: <a href="https://afrosonics.tumblr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Harmony Holiday's Afrosonics archive</a>. A deep Black sonic repository of music, fragments, recordings, interviews, memory, and cultural atmosphere. Useful less as a "source list" than as a model for how sound can behave as <strong>archive, collage, inheritance, interruption, and survival</strong>.</p>
  <p>Connect this to THE MISSING and Cosmic Archaeology: fragments as surviving material, fragments as code, fragments as pathways between past, present, and future knowledge. Treat it as a living sonic repository and a possible orientation point, not a public link to share.</p>
  <span class="ref-stamp">Internal reference / discreet / not for circulation</span>
</div>

<div class="closing">
  <p>This document is the first bridge. The world is bigger than any single brief can hold, and we will keep building it together. Bring me the obvious things. Bring me the buried ones. Bring me the fragment, the unfinished take, the song that might not even be a song, the breath that became a track, the bassline that arrived in a dream. Bring me what you cannot explain.</p>
  <p>The sonic register of this film is equal to the visual register. It is not décor. It is architecture. I am leading it firmly, and I am inviting you in fully. There is room here. There is real room.</p>
  <p>Antoinette flies home at the end. Every sound we choose, every silence we hold, is a step toward that homecoming. Hold the work with that weight. I am looking forward to what you bring.</p>

